[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_impl_pretense.py: The call_target pivot added for allocated in this change (lines 95-100) does not take effect for the real allocator: the checked and fuzzed allocator executes the inherited interface-model allocated transition, which asserts the SUT cumulative allocation equals the canonical model value. Because an implementation pseudo-state machine only observes the SUT through call_target and must not advance the model (PN_IMPL_NO_STATE_MUTATION), that assertion fails once funds have been allocated: TestInterInterfaceImplReal expects allocated == 25 after allocate(40), release(15), and a gated allocate(500), and InterInterfaceFuzzTest fails on the counterexample drawing False then 1 over two rule-method steps. inter_interface.pyi requires allocated to report the current cumulative allocation, yet the executed transition raises AssertionError instead of returning it.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: The call_target pivot added for withdraw in this change (lines 54-68) does not take effect for the real vault: the checked vault executes the inherited interface-model withdraw transition, whose require_arg domain is derived from the canonical model balance that an implementation pseudo-state machine must not advance (PN_IMPL_NO_STATE_MUTATION). Consequently TestVaultImplReal.test_real_conformance fails on the contract-valid full-balance withdrawal of 65 (after deposit(100), withdraw(40), and deposit(5)) with a PretenseSpecificationError from domain validation before the SUT is ever exercised, even though vault.pyi requires that any 0 < amount <= balance be withdrawable.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_pretense.py: Fix feedback: withdraw require_arg domain now accepts the full balance (exclusive upper bound +1), and interface property transitions (balance/is_active) no longer assert equality against canonical model state so checked SUT values are returned.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/pretense/inter_interface_pretense.py: Fix feedback: release require_arg domain now accepts the full allocated amount (exclusive upper bound +1), and the allocated property transition no longer asserts equality against canonical model state so the checked SUT cumulative allocation is returned.
