[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: The TestVaultImplReal.test_real_conformance scenario at lines 126-133 drains the vault to a zero balance with withdraw(65) and then, after set_active(False), calls withdraw(10) and expects VaultInactiveException. vault.pyi makes 0 < amount <= balance a withdraw precondition, so withdrawing 10 against a zero balance is a caller precondition violation whose contracted outcome is the checked *Error InsufficientFundsError, not the operational VaultInactiveException postcondition; the interface-model change that widened the domain to permit the full-balance withdrawal of 65 does not make this later call legal, and the model precondition gate correctly rejects it. The inactive-vault postcondition must be exercised with a remaining balance at least as large as the requested withdrawal, so the scenario must not drain the vault before toggling it inactive.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/pretense/vault_impl_pretense.py: Fix feedback: TestVaultImplReal.test_real_conformance no longer drains the vault before toggling it inactive. It now withdraws 25 (leaving balance 40), exercises the inactive-vault VaultInactiveException postconditions with withdraw(10) and deposit(10) while the withdraw precondition 0 < amount <= balance remains satisfied, asserts the balance is unchanged, then re-activates and performs a contract-valid full-balance withdrawal of 40 followed by deposit(7).
