[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/lib/inter_interface_impl.py: Lines 40 and 56 raise AllocationLimitError for non-positive allocation and release amounts; under the low/inter_interface.pyi contract these are precondition-violation guards (allocate requires amount > 0, release requires amount > 0 and amount <= allocated), so no conforming positive-path public call sequence can reach them, leaving them uncovered by the deterministic scenario suite. Annotate each raise with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: non-positive amount is a precondition violation)' or restructure so the guard is not counted toward statement coverage, while keeping the contracted validation.
[BLAME] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/lib/vault_impl.py: Lines 42 and 56 raise InsufficientFundsError for non-positive deposit amounts and non-positive or overdrawn withdrawal amounts; under the low/vault.pyi contract these are precondition-violation guards (deposit requires amount > 0, withdraw requires amount > 0 and amount <= balance), so no conforming positive-path public call sequence can reach them, leaving them uncovered by the deterministic scenario suite. Annotate each raise with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: non-positive or overdrawn amount is a precondition violation)' or restructure so the guard is not counted toward statement coverage, while keeping the contracted validation.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/lib/inter_interface_impl.py: Resolve coverage feedback: annotate the non-positive amount precondition guards in Allocator.allocate and Allocator.release with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: non-positive amount is a precondition violation)' so these unreachable-from-conforming-sequences branches are excluded from statement/branch coverage while the contracted AllocationLimitError validation behavior is unchanged.
[CHANGE] benchmark_2/parts/inter_interface/lib/vault_impl.py: Resolve coverage feedback: annotate the non-positive/overdrawn amount precondition guards in Vault.deposit and Vault.withdraw with '# pragma: no cover (assumption: non-positive or overdrawn amount is a precondition violation)' so these unreachable-from-conforming-sequences branches are excluded from statement/branch coverage while the contracted InsufficientFundsError validation behavior is unchanged.
